  "review": {
    "review": "This was a living-hero planner failure, not a death. Decision 3172's accepted transition (log 9272) reaches doorway 1150. Decision 3173 (log 9274) publicly observes exit 1074, summoning trap 1114, upgrade scroll 1155 and a sleeping thief at 1156; known levitation is already carried. The bot retreats and continues other exploration. The initiating blocker is therefore not simply failure to discover stairs: the observed stair approach is quarantined with a mixed chasm/trap chamber. tools/summoning_tactics.py:71-87 floods the observed chamber; tools/special_rooms.py:103-107 excludes it, and tools/survival_policy.py:436-465 removes its approach from ordinary paths. Deliberate summoning preparation refuses floors beyond four. Flight preparation also has independent health, actor, route and room-exclusion requirements; its existing journey controller plans loot round trips, not protected stair transitions. Reduced public-snapshot helper probes reproduce the excluded approach and declining preparation, but are not recorded runtime memory. A complete historical policy-state reconstruction was attempted but is not certified here. At decision 3305, accepted log 9653 confirms healing from 44 to 62 HP while remaining at 1104; decision 3306, log 9654, exhausts planning with the hero alive. Four starving wall searches and last-resort healing are downstream symptoms. No patch or regression is submitted: a safe protected itinerary preserving mandatory upgrade pickup, actual levitation verification, fresh enemy checks and interruption/return handling has not been established. Simply allowing chamber entry, treating stairs as loot, increasing search limits or bypassing quarantine would not supply that contract. Source browsing resolves the omitted-exit and selecting-chain ambiguity, but does not certify a safe replacement.",
    "learnings": "Distinguish an unobserved exit from an observed exit whose approach is excluded. Investigate the chamber's protection and pickup transaction before spending missing-exit searches. Known levitation is a preparation resource, not evidence that a hazardous crossing or mandatory pickup has succeeded."
  },
